Clean-room notice
-----------------
This project is a clean-room, native Python reimplementation of the TP-Link
Archer AX53 v1 web-UI authentication and request protocol. It was written from
two first-party reference documents produced by observing and executing the
router's own static JavaScript bundle offline:

  * docs/specs/archer-ax53-auth-flow.md  (the protocol, tagged [V]/[O]/[I])
  * tests/fixtures/router_auth_vectors.json  (byte-exact vectors)

The GPL-3.0 project `tplinkrouterc6u` (notably `client/sg.py`) was consulted
**only** to cross-check observed behaviour. No code, comments, structure, or
other copyrightable expression from that project was copied, adapted, or
incorporated here. This repository contains no GPL-licensed code and is
distributable under the MIT License.

Test vectors
------------
`tests/fixtures/router_auth_vectors.json` contains a throwaway RSA private key
and dummy inputs (password "TestPass123") generated offline for deterministic
crypto tests. No real device credentials, keys, addresses, or hardware
identifiers appear anywhere in this repository.
